1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:01,448
December 9, 1959.

2
00:00:01,448 --> 00:00:08,047
In a hall in Munich, hundreds of shareholders are about to vote on the end of BMW.

3
00:00:10,616 --> 00:00:13,485
The plan is to sell it to its biggest rival:

4
00:00:13,485 --> 00:00:14,398
Mercedes-Benz.

5
00:00:14,398 --> 00:00:18,636
The bank that controls BMW's debt already sees it as a done deal.

6
00:00:18,933 --> 00:00:22,281
But that night, something nobody expected happens.

7
00:00:22,281 --> 00:00:27,704
And sixty-six years later, BMW sells more cars under its brand than Mercedes, and

8
00:00:27,704 --> 00:00:29,043
makes billions more.

9
00:00:29,123 --> 00:00:33,948
How did it go from the brink of disappearing to one of the most desired brands on

10
00:00:33,948 --> 00:00:34,604
the planet?

11
00:00:34,684 --> 00:00:39,956
This story has aircraft engines, motorcycles, cooking pots, a car shaped like an

12
00:00:39,956 --> 00:00:42,790
egg, and the worst purchase in its history.

13
00:00:42,870 --> 00:00:44,792
And it also has a dark side.

14
00:00:44,792 --> 00:00:50,420
The family that saved BMW, and a past that took more than sixty years to come out.

15
00:00:51,132 --> 00:00:53,483
This is the full story of BMW.

16
00:00:53,483 --> 00:00:57,009
From the sky, to near bankruptcy, to the top.

17
00:00:58,194 --> 00:00:59,321
Chapter one.

18
00:00:59,321 --> 00:01:01,198
Engines for the sky.

19
00:01:01,497 --> 00:01:04,572
Munich, in the middle of the First World War.

20
00:01:04,572 --> 00:01:07,715
Germany needs planes, and planes need engines.

21
00:01:09,031 --> 00:01:15,300
BMW counts March 7, 1916 as its birthday, when an aircraft factory is founded in

22
00:01:15,300 --> 00:01:15,849
Munich.

23
00:01:19,360 --> 00:01:25,924
Nearby, another company, Rapp Motorenwerke, builds aircraft engines.

24
00:01:25,924 --> 00:01:28,626
In 1917 it changes its name:

25
00:01:28,626 --> 00:01:31,039
Bayerische Motoren Werke.

26
00:01:31,039 --> 00:01:33,066
Bavarian Motor Works.

27
00:01:33,066 --> 00:01:33,452
BMW.

28
00:01:33,532 --> 00:01:38,269
Its first big product is designed by an engineer named Max Friz:

29
00:01:38,269 --> 00:01:40,934
an aircraft engine, the BMW three A.

30
00:01:41,014 --> 00:01:43,489
Its advantage was huge for the time:

31
00:01:43,489 --> 00:01:48,851
at altitude, where the air is thinner, it performed better than rival engines.

32
00:01:48,931 --> 00:01:51,235
And the logo comes from those years.

33
00:01:51,235 --> 00:01:55,844
For decades, people said it was a propeller spinning against a blue sky.

34
00:01:55,924 --> 00:01:56,405
But no.

35
00:01:56,405 --> 00:02:02,175
The circle comes from Rapp's logo, and the blue and white are the colors of Bavaria.

36
00:02:02,175 --> 00:02:07,053
The propeller story only appeared in the late twenties, in advertising.

37
00:02:07,133 --> 00:02:09,438
Then the war ends, and Germany loses.

38
00:02:09,438 --> 00:02:13,864
The Treaty of Versailles bans Germany from having a military air force.

39
00:02:13,944 --> 00:02:19,374
For a company that lived on making aircraft engines, that's a death sentence.

40
00:02:19,374 --> 00:02:21,702
BMW has to invent a new business.

41
00:02:22,622 --> 00:02:23,597
Chapter two.

42
00:02:23,597 --> 00:02:25,548
Two wheels, four wheels.

43
00:02:25,977 --> 00:02:30,143
In 1923, BMW unveils its first motorcycle:

44
00:02:30,143 --> 00:02:31,829
the R thirty-two.

45
00:02:32,623 --> 00:02:34,155
It had a boxer engine:

46
00:02:34,155 --> 00:02:37,778
two cylinders lying flat, sticking out on each side.

47
00:02:37,778 --> 00:02:41,818
They're cooled by the air and lower the center of gravity.

48
00:02:41,898 --> 00:02:46,856
A hundred years later, BMW still builds motorcycles with that same idea.

49
00:02:46,856 --> 00:02:48,716
It's one of its trademarks.

50
00:02:49,623 --> 00:02:52,386
But motorcycles aren't enough.

51
00:02:52,386 --> 00:02:53,768
BMW wants cars.

52
00:02:53,768 --> 00:02:56,807
And in 1928, it finds a shortcut.

53
00:02:56,896 --> 00:03:02,809
It buys a factory in Eisenach, in central Germany, that made a small car called the

54
00:03:02,809 --> 00:03:03,165
Dixi.

55
00:03:03,245 --> 00:03:04,546
The funny detail:

56
00:03:04,546 --> 00:03:06,995
the Dixi wasn't a German design.

57
00:03:06,995 --> 00:03:10,899
It was a licensed copy of the British Austin Seven.

58
00:03:10,979 --> 00:03:16,541
So the first car with the BMW name, the three fifteen, was really an English car

59
00:03:16,541 --> 00:03:18,140
with a different badge.

60
00:03:18,220 --> 00:03:20,917
During the thirties, BMW learns fast.

61
00:03:20,917 --> 00:03:25,726
Its cars earn a reputation for being sporty, light and well built.

62
00:03:25,806 --> 00:03:28,020
And then another war comes.

63
00:03:28,020 --> 00:03:32,938
And with it, the part of the story BMW took decades to tell.

64
00:03:33,962 --> 00:03:35,281
Chapter three.

65
00:03:35,281 --> 00:03:37,541
The part BMW kept quiet.

66
00:03:38,101 --> 00:03:42,970
During the Second World War, BMW goes back to what it does best:

67
00:03:42,970 --> 00:03:44,263
aircraft engines.

68
00:03:44,263 --> 00:03:46,774
This time, for Hitler's military.

69
00:03:48,012 --> 00:03:51,568
To meet production targets, there aren't enough workers.

70
00:03:51,568 --> 00:03:53,981
And the company turns to forced labor.

71
00:03:54,061 --> 00:03:55,831
That's not us saying it.

72
00:03:55,831 --> 00:03:58,781
BMW itself says it today on its website:

73
00:03:58,781 --> 00:04:04,608
its management had no qualms about using forced laborers and concentration camp

74
00:04:04,608 --> 00:04:05,346
prisoners.

75
00:04:05,426 --> 00:04:11,406
In 1943, next to one of its plants, the Allach camp is set up, a subcamp of the

76
00:04:11,406 --> 00:04:13,374
Dachau concentration camp.

77
00:04:13,374 --> 00:04:16,554
Prisoners worked up to twelve hours a day.

78
00:04:18,345 --> 00:04:24,269
Like almost every German company, BMW denied its responsibility for a long time.

79
00:04:24,269 --> 00:04:29,526
Since 2020, its museum in Munich has a space dedicated to this chapter.

80
00:04:30,895 --> 00:04:35,623
And when the war ends, in 1945, BMW is in ruins.

81
00:04:38,009 --> 00:04:38,982
Chapter four.

82
00:04:38,982 --> 00:04:41,902
Pots, motorcycles and an egg on wheels.

83
00:04:42,279 --> 00:04:45,164
The Munich halls are bombed or dismantled.

84
00:04:45,164 --> 00:04:48,941
And the Eisenach car factory ends up on the other side:

85
00:04:48,941 --> 00:04:50,246
in the Soviet zone.

86
00:04:51,589 --> 00:04:58,319
There, the Soviets keep the factory, and for years they build cars from BMW designs

87
00:04:58,319 --> 00:04:59,859
under another name:

88
00:04:59,859 --> 00:05:00,183
EMW.

89
00:05:01,317 --> 00:05:04,316
BMW is left without a car factory.

90
00:05:04,316 --> 00:05:07,226
So what does it do to stay alive?

91
00:05:07,226 --> 00:05:07,667
Pots.

92
00:05:07,667 --> 00:05:08,108
Pans.

93
00:05:08,108 --> 00:05:09,166
Kitchenware.

94
00:05:09,246 --> 00:05:10,609
The idea was simple:

95
00:05:10,609 --> 00:05:15,516
keep its skilled workers busy until it could build something real again.

96
00:05:17,037 --> 00:05:19,685
In 1948, motorcycles return.

97
00:05:19,685 --> 00:05:23,088
And in 1951, the first post-war car:

98
00:05:23,088 --> 00:05:24,979
the BMW five oh one.

99
00:05:27,497 --> 00:05:30,389
It was a big, luxurious, expensive sedan.

100
00:05:30,389 --> 00:05:36,104
The problem was that Germany in the fifties was in ruins, and almost nobody could

101
00:05:36,104 --> 00:05:36,809
afford it.

102
00:05:36,889 --> 00:05:42,943
Then, at the 1954 Turin Motor Show, someone from BMW sees something strange:

103
00:05:42,943 --> 00:05:46,528
a tiny, round car with its door at the front.

104
00:05:48,076 --> 00:05:53,011
It was called the Isetta, it was made by an Italian company called Iso, and to get

105
00:05:53,011 --> 00:05:55,899
in, you had to open the entire front of the car.

106
00:05:55,979 --> 00:06:00,952
BMW buys the license, and from 1955 it builds its own Isetta.

107
00:06:00,952 --> 00:06:03,398
People call it the bubble car.

108
00:06:05,442 --> 00:06:09,734
It's cheap, it barely uses any fuel, and it saves thousands of jobs in Munich.

109
00:06:09,734 --> 00:06:12,926
Workers who built motorcycles move on to building Isettas.

110
00:06:13,006 --> 00:06:14,992
But BMW has a deeper problem.

111
00:06:14,992 --> 00:06:19,719
The luxury cars lose money, and the cheap ones don't bring in enough.

112
00:06:20,431 --> 00:06:21,817
The debts pile up.

113
00:06:21,817 --> 00:06:26,282
And by the late fifties, BMW is on the edge of bankruptcy.

114
00:06:27,885 --> 00:06:29,005
Chapter five.

115
00:06:29,005 --> 00:06:31,072
The night of December 9.

116
00:06:31,946 --> 00:06:32,322
1959.

117
00:06:32,322 --> 00:06:38,633
BMW owes a huge amount of money to Deutsche Bank, the most powerful bank in Germany.

118
00:06:40,420 --> 00:06:45,227
And the bank's man on BMW's board, Hans Feith, has a plan:

119
00:06:45,227 --> 00:06:50,033
Daimler-Benz, the owner of Mercedes, should take over BMW.

120
00:06:51,350 --> 00:06:55,619
According to BMW itself, the sale seemed like a done deal.

121
00:06:55,619 --> 00:07:00,035
BMW was going to be, at best, just another Mercedes factory.

122
00:07:00,115 --> 00:07:04,125
On December 9, the shareholders' meeting is held in Munich.

123
00:07:04,125 --> 00:07:06,503
The choice they're given is brutal:

124
00:07:06,503 --> 00:07:08,135
Mercedes, or bankruptcy.

125
00:07:08,637 --> 00:07:13,024
But in the room, there are people who aren't willing to give up.

126
00:07:13,024 --> 00:07:15,560
Small shareholders, dealers, workers.

127
00:07:16,119 --> 00:07:21,024
One of them is Erich Nold, a small shareholder who starts dragging out the meeting

128
00:07:21,024 --> 00:07:22,819
with questions and objections.

129
00:07:22,899 --> 00:07:28,445
Another is Friedrich Mathern, a lawyer representing dealers, who arrives with legal

130
00:07:28,445 --> 00:07:32,120
arguments against the accounts presented by management.

131
00:07:32,200 --> 00:07:36,206
And in the room, someone mentions a figure that changes everything:

132
00:07:36,206 --> 00:07:41,108
BMW's new small model, the seven hundred, already has twenty-five thousand orders.

133
00:07:41,802 --> 00:07:47,050
After hours of debate, the opponents gather enough shares to stop the vote.

134
00:07:47,050 --> 00:07:49,639
The sale to Mercedes is not approved.

135
00:07:50,511 --> 00:07:51,981
BMW is still alive.

136
00:07:51,981 --> 00:07:53,295
But only for now:

137
00:07:53,295 --> 00:07:56,389
without money, that delay means nothing.

138
00:07:57,392 --> 00:08:01,224
And that's when the key figure of this story appears:

139
00:08:01,224 --> 00:08:06,430
Herbert Quandt, an industrialist who already owned a large stake in BMW.

140
00:08:06,650 --> 00:08:07,764
Accounts differ.

141
00:08:07,764 --> 00:08:11,387
Some say Quandt first supported the sale to Daimler.

142
00:08:11,387 --> 00:08:15,009
But in the end, he changes his mind and bets on BMW.

143
00:08:16,012 --> 00:08:21,374
In 1960, he backs a rescue plan with a capital increase, and his family ends up

144
00:08:21,374 --> 00:08:23,614
owning close to half the company.

145
00:08:25,817 --> 00:08:26,927
Chapter six.

146
00:08:26,927 --> 00:08:28,221
The New Class.

147
00:08:28,886 --> 00:08:34,400
The seven hundred, designed with the Italian Giovanni Michelotti, sells well and

148
00:08:34,400 --> 00:08:37,088
gives BMW the breathing room it needed.

149
00:08:37,168 --> 00:08:42,577
But the real bet is unveiled at the 1961 Frankfurt Motor Show:

150
00:08:42,577 --> 00:08:44,671
the BMW fifteen hundred.

151
00:08:44,671 --> 00:08:45,893
The New Class.

152
00:08:47,401 --> 00:08:50,485
People waited in line for half an hour to see it.

153
00:08:50,485 --> 00:08:54,323
It was a modern, mid-size sedan that drove like a sports car.

154
00:08:54,935 --> 00:08:56,088
And one detail:

155
00:08:56,088 --> 00:09:02,469
when Quandt saw the finished design, he asked to bring back the twin kidney grille.

156
00:09:02,469 --> 00:09:05,083
The same one BMW still uses today.

157
00:09:05,163 --> 00:09:08,951
With the New Class, BMW finally finds its place:

158
00:09:08,951 --> 00:09:11,634
cars for people who love to drive.

159
00:09:11,634 --> 00:09:16,291
Not the heavy luxury of Mercedes, not everyone's cheap car.

160
00:09:16,371 --> 00:09:20,500
In 1972, its performance division, BMW M, is born.

161
00:09:20,500 --> 00:09:24,713
And the next year it opens its Munich headquarters:

162
00:09:24,713 --> 00:09:27,603
a tower shaped like four cylinders.

163
00:09:28,611 --> 00:09:34,959
In 1975, the 3 Series arrives, and over the years it becomes its most important car.

164
00:09:35,727 --> 00:09:41,135
And in the United States, a small agency comes up with a slogan it still uses:

165
00:09:41,135 --> 00:09:43,146
The Ultimate Driving Machine.

166
00:09:46,526 --> 00:09:47,375
It worked.

167
00:09:47,375 --> 00:09:53,063
In 1974, BMW sold about fifteen thousand cars in the United States.

168
00:09:53,063 --> 00:09:57,053
Two years later, more than twenty-six thousand.

169
00:09:57,133 --> 00:10:02,641
The company that in 1959 almost ended up as a Mercedes factory was now competing

170
00:10:02,641 --> 00:10:04,500
head to head with Mercedes.

171
00:10:06,164 --> 00:10:07,225
Chapter seven.

172
00:10:07,225 --> 00:10:09,273
The silence of the Quandts.

173
00:10:09,885 --> 00:10:13,877
Herbert Quandt died in 1982 as the man who saved BMW.

174
00:10:13,877 --> 00:10:17,644
But his family was keeping a story it didn't tell.

175
00:10:19,274 --> 00:10:24,501
In 2007, German television aired a documentary with a blunt title:

176
00:10:24,501 --> 00:10:26,640
The Silence of the Quandts.

177
00:10:26,729 --> 00:10:32,055
Under pressure, the family commissioned an independent study from historian Joachim

178
00:10:32,055 --> 00:10:32,826
Scholtyseck.

179
00:10:32,826 --> 00:10:37,125
It was published in 2011, and it ran to about twelve hundred pages.

180
00:10:37,240 --> 00:10:39,184
The conclusions were harsh.

181
00:10:39,184 --> 00:10:44,942
In the factories of Herbert's father, Günther Quandt, some fifty thousand forced

182
00:10:44,942 --> 00:10:47,533
laborers worked during the Nazi era.

183
00:10:47,883 --> 00:10:51,385
Those factories made batteries and weapons for the regime.

184
00:10:51,385 --> 00:10:55,732
And the family had taken over companies seized from their Jewish owners.

185
00:10:55,812 --> 00:11:01,221
The study concluded that Günther, and also Herbert, were responsible for numerous

186
00:11:01,221 --> 00:11:01,955
injustices.

187
00:11:01,955 --> 00:11:04,626
His son, Stefan Quandt, put it this way:

188
00:11:04,626 --> 00:11:06,897
his father was part of the system.

189
00:11:06,977 --> 00:11:08,921
An important clarification:

190
00:11:08,921 --> 00:11:11,298
the study does not implicate BMW.

191
00:11:11,298 --> 00:11:14,683
The family bought its BMW shares after the war.

192
00:11:16,492 --> 00:11:19,506
And there's an even more disturbing fact.

193
00:11:19,506 --> 00:11:22,815
Günther Quandt's second wife was named Magda.

194
00:11:22,815 --> 00:11:24,433
They divorced in 1929.

195
00:11:25,697 --> 00:11:31,093
Two years later, Magda married Joseph Goebbels, Hitler's propaganda minister.

196
00:11:31,093 --> 00:11:36,839
Her son with Günther, Harald Quandt, was the only one of her children who survived

197
00:11:36,839 --> 00:11:37,400
the war.

198
00:11:37,646 --> 00:11:43,564
Today, Herbert's children, Stefan Quandt and Susanne Klatten, own almost half of

199
00:11:43,564 --> 00:11:43,860
BMW.

200
00:11:43,860 --> 00:11:47,337
They're one of the richest families in Germany.

201
00:11:47,973 --> 00:11:48,926
Chapter eight.

202
00:11:48,926 --> 00:11:50,899
Ten pounds and a Rolls-Royce.

203
00:11:51,277 --> 00:11:52,325
Back to cars.

204
00:11:52,325 --> 00:11:58,853
In 1994, BMW wants to grow fast, and buys the British Rover Group for about eight

205
00:11:58,853 --> 00:12:00,707
hundred million pounds.

206
00:12:01,971 --> 00:12:04,144
It came with legendary brands:

207
00:12:04,144 --> 00:12:06,171
Rover, Land Rover, MG, Mini.

208
00:12:06,171 --> 00:12:08,488
It looked like the perfect move.

209
00:12:08,568 --> 00:12:09,786
It was a disaster.

210
00:12:09,786 --> 00:12:15,198
Rover lost money year after year, and the losses started dragging down the whole

211
00:12:15,198 --> 00:12:15,604
group.

212
00:12:15,684 --> 00:12:17,474
In 2000, BMW gives up.

213
00:12:17,474 --> 00:12:19,753
It sells Land Rover to Ford.

214
00:12:19,753 --> 00:12:20,567
And Rover?

215
00:12:20,567 --> 00:12:25,368
It sells it to a group of businessmen for a symbolic price:

216
00:12:25,368 --> 00:12:26,264
ten pounds.

217
00:12:26,479 --> 00:12:30,480
And on top of that, it lends them five hundred and fifty million pounds

218
00:12:30,480 --> 00:12:31,269
interest-free.

219
00:12:31,269 --> 00:12:34,537
Buying Rover was the worst decision in its modern history.

220
00:12:34,617 --> 00:12:38,361
From that whole disaster, BMW keeps just one thing:

221
00:12:38,361 --> 00:12:39,462
the Mini brand.

222
00:12:39,462 --> 00:12:44,161
And in 2001 it launches a new Mini that becomes a worldwide hit.

223
00:12:44,241 --> 00:12:49,188
Meanwhile, it pulls off one of the smartest moves in the industry.

224
00:12:49,188 --> 00:12:52,861
In 1998, Rolls-Royce Motor Cars goes up for sale.

225
00:12:52,941 --> 00:12:57,397
Volkswagen wins the auction and gets the factory in Crewe, England.

226
00:12:57,397 --> 00:12:59,724
But there was one detail it missed.

227
00:12:59,804 --> 00:13:03,656
The Rolls-Royce name and logo didn't belong to the car company.

228
00:13:03,656 --> 00:13:07,080
They belonged to Rolls-Royce, the aircraft engine maker.

229
00:13:07,080 --> 00:13:10,933
And that company licenses them to BMW for forty million pounds.

230
00:13:11,226 --> 00:13:11,976
The result:

231
00:13:11,976 --> 00:13:17,222
Volkswagen keeps Bentley, and since 2003, Rolls-Royces have been made by BMW.

232
00:13:17,222 --> 00:13:22,945
The company that started with aircraft engines won the name from the aircraft engine

233
00:13:22,945 --> 00:13:23,490
company.

234
00:13:24,140 --> 00:13:25,168
Chapter nine.

235
00:13:25,168 --> 00:13:27,380
The return of the New Class.

236
00:13:27,679 --> 00:13:33,503
Today, the BMW Group, with Mini and Rolls-Royce, delivers close to two and a half

237
00:13:33,503 --> 00:13:35,228
million vehicles a year.

238
00:13:35,369 --> 00:13:40,900
And in 2025, something happened that in 1959 would have sounded like science

239
00:13:40,900 --> 00:13:41,482
fiction.

240
00:13:42,433 --> 00:13:46,890
The BMW brand sold two point one seven million cars.

241
00:13:46,890 --> 00:13:50,920
Mercedes-Benz, about two point one six million.

242
00:13:50,920 --> 00:13:51,863
BMW, ahead.

243
00:13:53,780 --> 00:13:55,841
And in profits, even more:

244
00:13:55,841 --> 00:13:59,568
BMW made almost seven and a half billion euros.

245
00:13:59,568 --> 00:14:02,818
Mercedes, about five point three billion.

246
00:14:04,292 --> 00:14:06,899
That doesn't mean everything is fine.

247
00:14:06,899 --> 00:14:12,676
Its revenue fell more than six percent, it's struggling in China and with tariffs,

248
00:14:12,676 --> 00:14:14,649
and it expects a tough 2026.

249
00:14:14,729 --> 00:14:18,703
But it arrives better prepared than many for the electric era.

250
00:14:18,703 --> 00:14:23,767
In 2025, it sold more than four hundred and forty thousand fully electric cars.

251
00:14:24,009 --> 00:14:26,505
In May 2026, it changed bosses:

252
00:14:26,505 --> 00:14:33,028
Oliver Zipse left after thirty-five years, and Milan Nedeljković, the head of its

253
00:14:33,028 --> 00:14:34,719
factories, took over.

254
00:14:35,069 --> 00:14:38,973
And its big bet for the future has a familiar name.

255
00:14:38,973 --> 00:14:43,872
BMW's new generation of electric cars is called the Neue Klasse.

256
00:14:43,872 --> 00:14:44,943
The New Class.

257
00:14:45,215 --> 00:14:48,631
The same name as the car that saved it in 1961.

258
00:14:48,631 --> 00:14:50,230
That's no coincidence:

259
00:14:50,230 --> 00:14:54,227
it's BMW's way of saying it's betting everything again.

260
00:14:55,831 --> 00:14:59,135
If there's anything to take from this story, it's three things.

261
00:14:59,215 --> 00:14:59,707
First:

262
00:14:59,707 --> 00:15:03,397
a company can reinvent itself more than once.

263
00:15:03,397 --> 00:15:08,645
Aircraft engines, motorcycles, pots, bubble cars, sports sedans.

264
00:15:09,174 --> 00:15:09,691
Second:

265
00:15:09,691 --> 00:15:15,519
sometimes everything comes down to one night, and to a few people who refuse to

266
00:15:15,519 --> 00:15:15,888
sign.

267
00:15:15,968 --> 00:15:16,766
And third:

268
00:15:16,766 --> 00:15:19,241
success doesn't erase the past.

269
00:15:19,241 --> 00:15:23,073
BMW and the Quandts took decades to tell theirs.

270
00:15:23,562 --> 00:15:24,835
Now I'm asking you.

271
00:15:24,835 --> 00:15:25,908
BMW or Mercedes?

272
00:15:25,908 --> 00:15:29,392
And which company should we cover in the next video?

273
00:15:29,392 --> 00:15:31,268
Let me know in the comments.

274
00:15:31,514 --> 00:15:34,975
If you liked it, subscribe and turn on notifications.

275
00:15:34,975 --> 00:15:36,000
Thanks for watching to the end.

276
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:38,567
See you in the next one.

